  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Normal stool pH (6.5 &ndash; 7.5):</strong>&nbsp;Indicates normal digestion and absorption.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Acidic stool pH (&lt; 5.5):</strong>&nbsp;May indicate carbohydrate malabsorption, lactose intolerance, or intestinal infections causing fermentation; common in infants and diarrheal states.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Alkaline stool pH (&gt; 7.5):</strong> May be associated with bacterial overgrowth, bile salt malabsorption, or conditions like colitis.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
